The Palawan bearded pig (_Sus ahoenobarbus_) has formerly been considered a subspecies of the bearded pig. However, as indicated by its genetic and morphological distinctness, under the phylogenetic species concept (which does not use subspecies) it needs to be elevated to full species status; while the situation is less clear under other species concepts (as not all _S. barbatus_ populations have been restudied in modern times), the presently available information seems to favor full species status for _S. ahoenobarbus_ in any case.

